menu "breadboard: bb_wifi_prov"

config BB_WIFI_PROV_TASK_STACK
    int "Provisioning manager task stack size (bytes)"
    default 6144
    range 4096 16384
    help
        Stack for the wifi_prov_mgr task that drives the WP_IDLE/WP_ACTIVE/
        WP_CLOSING provisioning FSM (wifi_prov_policy.h). PROVISIONAL AND
        UNMEASURED -- no on-device stack-high-water-mark reading has been
        taken for this task yet.

        See wifi_reconn's own RECONN_TASK_STACK comment
        (platform/espidf/bb_wifi/wifi_reconn.c) for the precedent this
        guesses from: that task shipped at 4096 and only later, after a real
        bug (B1-330), was raised to 6144 once the escalate-reboot path's NVS
        writes were measured to consume ~1.5-2 KB more stack than assumed.
        Don't repeat that mistake here without measuring.

        To measure: flash, let the manager task run through at least one
        WP_ACTIVE (portal open) cycle, then GET /api/diag/tasks and read
        stack_hwm for "wifi_prov_mgr" (every FreeRTOS task is reported
        automatically -- see bb_diag_tasks_get_wire_fill_row's
        usStackHighWaterMark field, platform/espidf/bb_diag_http/
        bb_diag_http_routes.c). Adjust this default once real numbers exist.

        Defaulted to 6144 (not wifi_reconn's original 4096) because this
        task's peak call path is heavier: act_try_ap_start/act_try_prov_start
        run esp_wifi/esp_netif AP init plus httpd_start (bb_wifi_prov_start),
        which is a deeper/heavier call chain than the NVS-write path that
        forced wifi_reconn up from 4096.

config BB_WIFI_PROV_TASK_PRIORITY
    int "Provisioning manager task priority"
    default 5
    range 1 20
    help
        FreeRTOS priority for the wifi_prov_mgr task. Default 5: matches
        wifi_reconn's RECONN_TASK_PRIO peer-manager task, above background
        worker tasks (1), well below the esp_timer service task (~22).

config BB_WIFI_PROV_QUEUE_DEPTH
    int "Provisioning manager event queue depth"
    default 8
    range 4 32
    help
        Depth of the queue between the provisioning-entry/save-success
        notifiers and the wifi_prov_mgr task. Matches wifi_reconn's
        RECONN_QUEUE_LEN peer default.

config BB_WIFI_PROV_SETTLE_MS
    int "WP_CLOSING settle-timer duration (ms)"
    default 2000
    range 100 30000
    help
        How long the provisioning FSM waits in WP_CLOSING (see
        wifi_prov_policy.h) before tearing down the portal after a
        successful POST /save, giving the in-flight HTTP response time to
        flush before ap_stop_fn tears the netif out from under it.

        Floored at 100, never 0: bb_fsm_arm_timer(fsm, event, ms==0)
        DISARMS rather than fires (bb_fsm.h), and the settle timeout is
        WP_CLOSING's ONLY exit -- a 0 here would strand the FSM (and the
        portal/AP) in WP_CLOSING forever. wifi_prov_policy.c's
        settle_ms_floor() also floors defensively at the point of use, but
        this Kconfig range is the first line of defense against a
        misconfigured build ever producing that value.

endmenu
